@startuml
title SysMon - Spawn LLM Server Activity Diagram

|Admin (Tier 1, 2 or 3)|
start
:Open LLM console;
:Paste HuggingFace model repository;
:Set context length,
CPU/GPU split and server port;
:Click Spawn;

|SysMon Backend|
:Ensure Ollama runtime is available;

if (Ollama installed?) then (No)
  :Install Ollama;
  if (Install succeeded?) then (No)
    :Notify admin that
    Ollama install failed;
    stop
  else (Yes)
  endif
else (Yes)
endif

:Estimate model resource requirements;
:Load admin's assigned Compute Group;

if (Model fits Compute Group
limits?) then (No)
  :Show Compute Group error
  (RAM / GPU / CPU exceeded);
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

if (Chosen port already in use?) then (Yes)
  :Notify admin that port is unavailable;
  stop
else (No)
endif

|Ollama|
:Start Ollama server on chosen port
with configured model and parameters;

|SysMon Backend|
if (Server started successfully?) then (No)
  :Notify admin of spawn failure;
  stop
else (Yes)
  :Register running LLM instance;
  |Admin (Tier 1, 2 or 3)|
  :View LLM console with
  listening endpoint;
  stop
endif

@enduml
